WEBVTT

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.980
Caption's all right, Joe.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.220
Read's plain enough.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.680
They'll buy them like hot kicks.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.020
Very good, another pressman.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.040
The soldiers are believing.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.280
Nah, they won't be leaving for over a week.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.720
The Army is parceling off the horses and wagons to the soldiers.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.150
Anything they can use to work on the farms when they get down home.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:29.870
General Lee gave his orders.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:59.970
this morning come on hop along we never will get home

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.530
What are you doing, Jeff?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.960
Retreating or advancing on the enemy.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.350
We don't know.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:07.820
Climb up here.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.660
You'll never get home on that, Jack.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:10.610
Thanks, Captain.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.330
Must have been full of cold liquor when you picked him out.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.340
I just took what they handed me.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.980
After straddling you for four years, I'll sure...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.100
Enjoy a steady seat.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.530
Somehow I can't get used to the war being over.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.440
I do think I'd be going home.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.140
Hope I'll never hear another shot fire as long as I live.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.420
And you going to Kentucky?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.290
I married into a feudal family,

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.290
but I'm not raising my children to become targets of a lot of bushwhackers.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.410
I'm going to move the family west.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:02:59.980
Just on a...

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:06.040
If a man can have some respect for his neighbors out there

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.300
and all the land you want for the asking,

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.270
that's where I'm going to build a permanent home for my family.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.540
You think you'll ever persuade Granny Spelman

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.440
and the old man to leave Kentucky?

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.720
How hard would you try to be your in-law?

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.890
That'll work out all right when I get home.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.970
Granny Spelman's been pretty good for my three children.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.640
since my wife died.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.930
How long is Lynn getting the date?

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:36.960
He's going on tape.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:56.830
Let me pack it, will you, Grampy?

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.700
Be careful now.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.960
My pop will be home for more than about five days, huh?

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.110
Think you'll know him, Lim?

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:13.970
Sure.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.730
Right fine eye.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.100
Easy to hit them when I pretend they're Colby's.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:29.800
Rabbit.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.940
It's ain't cold bears.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.610
The cold bears fight back.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:34.990
That's what makes them good hunting.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.060
Now my pappy can rest easy in his grave.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.940
I got Chet Spellman for him.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:18.390
Good, pappy.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:50.130
It's yours now, Lynn. Don't ever use it, excepting on a Colby.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:33.720
What's the matter?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.060
Why was your grandpappy?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:43.780
Why is he?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.230
He's down in Pineholler.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.380
He's laying there.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.500
He had coldly shot him.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.010
He doesn't run down to Wethersby's and tell him what's happened.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.450
Your papa will take care of Jed Colby when he gets here.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.120
I don't understand you, Mark Hayden.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.560
You've been home two weeks,

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.380
and Jed Colby straxing up and down these mountains,

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.970
bragging how he killed Chet Speldin.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:59.980
And here you are, backing up, running away.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.660
away from him. The law will take care of Colby. The law? It ain't honorable to take a family

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:16.440
feud to court that won't spill no blood for you. I want no blood spilled for me. Then

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:22.200
you're putting yourself above the prophets. A knife for a knife and a tooth for a tooth.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:25.130
It's in the book.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:41.510
It's your plain duty to take vengeance on Jed Colby.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.250
And then his kin is bound to take vengeance on me.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:47.800
And someday one of my sons must kill another Colby.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:52.350
No, I'm going to the law.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:08:59.980
Of course, Mark, if you...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.740
insist on preferring charges against Jed Colby, there's nothing I can say. I know it's procedure

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:12.570
in some places. It's up to the court to punish a man who commits a murder. That's a matter

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:22.360
of opinion. If you want him arrested, I'm bound to arrest him. Jed Colby, you have been found

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:28.900
guilty, but on account of the peculiar circumstances and feeling in this community, the court has

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.980
decided not to have a

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.570
hang on, but you'll have to go to the state penitentiary for 15 years for the murder of

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:58.640
Chet Spellick. Murder? Why, it was feudin', pure and simple. Had come out with it? He'd be coming out.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.860
Grandma's gone.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.180
She's dependent on him to do for her,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.500
and I couldn't take him away.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.040
You and Bill's got to be my family now.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.060
Those are mountains, Bill.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.970
The Kentucky hills are like woods alongside...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.320
But then, ain't they far?

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:02.540
They are, Bill.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:04.450
Jeff.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:05.150
Yep.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.410
Catch me those stakes.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:07.430
Come right up.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.110
Stick around the ground, son.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.010
You're getting out, Tuesday, Jed.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:48.320
Yeah.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:53.690
The daughter's waiting for you.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:55.400
I'll send her in.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.600
All right, miss.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:42.300
you can't travel west looking that way that's all I've got what do you want me to look like

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:59.980
sleeping in corners that's the first time

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:16.460
ever put your armor on me did did you find out where he's located i could go there with my eyes

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:24.050
Oh, my daughter, Ellen.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:29.780
Oh, I've never seen you before, huh?

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.400
Your father and I have been friends for several years.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.260
We had to be.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.000
We've been here together.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.840
I got out a few months ahead of him.

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:46.090
Going west with us?

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:47.240
Yes.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.020
You get $700.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:54.800
Good.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.670
That's enough to get an outfit with.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.030
Sure, I'll have everything ready.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.040
Get him.

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:34.120
We could have taken more than half that herd last night if you hadn't stopped us.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.340
The wolves get more of Hayden's cattle than we do.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.960
Yeah, we're taking enough.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.050
Not to suit me.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:53.550
A few hundred at a time ain't my idea of cattle rustling.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.960
We're going to strip Hayden of everything he's got before we get through.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.980
But we're going to do it my way.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.520
You've had your way for a year.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.840
The next time we raid that ranch, we'll run off enough stock to pay for the trouble.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:10.370
And keep on going till we've cleaned them out.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.590
But we won't be another year doing it.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.700
No, you won't until I'm ready.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.220
I'm stretching out his misery the same as he did mine.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:27.540
We're going to keep working on him till he comes gunning me.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.780
Oh, forget it.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.290
Let's get something out of this deal.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:33.750
Not yet.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:37.570
When I wipe out the Haydens, I'm going to get them all.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:42.580
What do you think I've been talking about?

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.220
There's one of me out here yet.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:45.830
The oldest boy.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.510
I'm not waiting for him.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.060
I'm going to have that Hayden ranch.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:55.870
Don't get your back up.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.680
I'm not leaving you out.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.100
I'm going to marry your daughter.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.130
Oh, ha, ha.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:05.180
There.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.370
If I may meet up your mind, that's the only way you can get her, eh?

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.070
I have her.

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:15.910
It's going to take a lot better man than you to tie that gal, Dag.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.240
Shoot off their guns.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.600
What'd you let her get on their horse for?

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:55.860
Oh, how was he gonna stop me?

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:56.680
Oh, you might have got chill.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:57.980
Now keep off them broncs.

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.980
She bet Daggs a kiss a...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.840
against something or other that she could ride the horse.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:03.360
Oh.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:36.760
Stop!

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:53.240
Where's Colby?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.390
Now, what's up?

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:55.070
The Hayden's shot.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:55.530
Keep down.

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.780
It's no more than a powder burn.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:14.630
Yes, sir.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.180
Think you killed him?

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.600
Yes. It was that fella, Pete Garren.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.010
It's Jed Colby's cousin.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:34.800
Darren was with Colby the day Grandpa Spellman was shot.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.120
Remember?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.490
What did you do it for, Neal?

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:42.200
You know Dad's been doing everything possible to keep from fighting with the Colbys.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.000
Dan, there's no use talking like that now.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.110
I told your father what happened.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.010
He was sure enough upset, but he doesn't blame me.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:52.960
Nobody's gonna shoot bullets into me if I can get him first.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:55.720
Well, that starts the old Kentucky feud boiling again.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.640
You keep out of this, Bill Hayden.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.970
I don't hanger to be a widow my first...

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:09.220
It's just fool's luck we're not all turning a hand to bury you what do you expect us to do set around let them move everything off the ranch

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:13.830
I've been telling you all along. They've been stealing more cattle than you'll ever admit

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:19.100
Colby's been doing everything to get dad fighting mad. Neil's right. We've got to face it sometime

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.680
Neil, come on. Dad's up to something.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:43.310
Where you going, Dad?

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:47.720
Talk to Jet Colby.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:49.500
Not alone.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:51.500
I don't need any help.

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:52.860
Bill and I are going with you.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.180
This is between the Haydens and the Colbys, Neil.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.460
My wife's a Hayden, isn't she?

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:16.850
What does it matter if you're a Hayden or a Colby, if a bullet gets you?

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:26.130
You drive off every head of stock from his ranch.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:29.470
By daybreak, there won't be a Hayden alive to stop you.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:42.900
For glass, Donnie!

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:25.750
I want to talk to you, Colby.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.860
My son-in-law got one of your men for stealing.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.360
my cattle. You can't accuse us of stealing cattle, to cover up the killing of Pete Geron. You've been

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:44.500
stealing cattle off my ranch for almost a year, doing all you can to start up that Colby Spelden

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:55.440
feud again. I'm not going feuding with you, Colby, but I am protecting what belongs to me. Hold it. Put

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:55.940
him on the table.

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:07.610
I've been after you.

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.950
I've got plenty of time.

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:41.960
I won't do it. You get out of here.

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:05.720
What happened to you?

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:06.940
And where'd you drop from?

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:12.080
I was just riding through, and all of a sudden I heard a splintering, and that dam tore loose.

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:13.620
And you were standing right in the way of it.

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:21.530
Dags, the boy sent me up to tell you they're waiting for whatever you're gonna do.

00:24:51.280 --> 00:24:52.100
Glad I happened by.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:57.000
Wouldn't have made much difference.

00:24:57.760 --> 00:24:59.320
I never seen the man I couldn't handle.

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:05.280
Better put your hat on before that sun hits you any worse.

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:06.180
Thanks, lady.

00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:15.040
Lady? What are you staring at?

00:25:16.460 --> 00:25:16.880
A lady?

00:25:18.070 --> 00:25:19.210
Now you're making fun of me.

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:20.420
No, I'm not.

00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:27.460
Where are you heading, Paul?

00:25:28.130 --> 00:25:29.910
Grass Valley. How much further?

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:36.720
is it? About seven hours with all them pack animals. You can't make it four dark sets

00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:46.820
in. You'll have to camp down the meadows for the night. Thanks, I will. Glad you asked

00:25:46.820 --> 00:25:55.120
by, stranger. You're welcome. What you thinking on, Ellen?

00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:05.460
Just wondering how ladies dress.

00:26:09.310 --> 00:26:15.160
Eli, what did your mother look like?

00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:18.080
Oh, she was beautiful.

00:26:20.920 --> 00:26:28.740
I remember one dress she had that had spangles all over it and feathers around the neck.

00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:33.440
She used to always carry a red pocketbook when she went out walking.

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:36.020
Do ladies wear their fine dresses all day?

00:26:36.440 --> 00:26:39.750
Oh, no. Only in the evening when the gentlemen come to court.

00:26:40.170 --> 00:26:40.890
And what did they do?

00:26:41.860 --> 00:26:46.400
Just sat around and talking and drinking and laughing.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:48.720
Having lots of fun in the big parlor.

00:26:48.940 --> 00:26:49.700
Did you live there?

00:26:50.090 --> 00:26:51.940
Me? Oh, no.

00:26:52.840 --> 00:26:54.460
We had a room just around the corner.

00:26:55.180 --> 00:26:58.060
But my mother used to always see her friends in the big house.

00:26:59.700 --> 00:26:59.980
They were...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:03.120
She didn't let me in the parlor. I was too young.

00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:06.280
But I used to peek through the curtain.

00:27:07.510 --> 00:27:10.420
Why, some of them ladies were lookers.

00:27:13.710 --> 00:27:17.640
I'd still be there if that sailor hadn't shot my mother.

00:27:24.030 --> 00:27:26.850
I wonder where we could get some shoes and stockings.

00:27:28.800 --> 00:27:29.480
Maybe a dress.

00:27:31.600 --> 00:27:33.080
And one of them feathered neck things.

00:27:33.650 --> 00:27:36.910
Well, maybe you can get them down at the store on Grass Valley.

00:27:37.430 --> 00:27:40.220
Oh, no. Besides, I want them for tonight.

00:27:44.510 --> 00:27:47.520
Guess I'll have to go walking just as I am.

00:28:09.530 --> 00:28:09.790
Hello.

00:28:14.080 --> 00:28:15.040
I saw your fire.

00:28:15.200 --> 00:28:15.740
Glad you did.

00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:17.040
I'll be through in a minute.

00:28:19.910 --> 00:28:20.970
Do you shave every day?

00:28:21.620 --> 00:28:22.260
Every other day.

00:28:23.690 --> 00:28:24.130
What for?

00:28:25.200 --> 00:28:26.240
Just a habit, I guess.

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:27.760
Why?

00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:34.400
I'd have thought you was kind of soft if I didn't see the strength in your arms.

00:29:01.500 --> 00:29:02.440
Will you have a cup of coffee?

00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:04.540
You're being polite and making fun of me.

00:29:05.280 --> 00:29:07.120
I ain't used to being polite at.

00:29:07.430 --> 00:29:10.090
I can get my own coffee without being waited on by men, folks.

00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:26.160
Must be sort of hard going barefoot through these mountains.

00:29:29.550 --> 00:29:29.970
It's none of your...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:40.290
business that i ain't got shoes and stockings i didn't mean anything that way they write poems

00:29:40.290 --> 00:29:47.030
about barefoot girls like you what's a poem oh a lot of words put together they don't mean anything

00:29:47.030 --> 00:29:55.020
but they sound pretty good want to hear one no i guess i wouldn't care for it i could sing your

00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:59.970
song i know a story about the indians you're gonna

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:11.170
to keep on making fun of me I'm going no don't now will you let me get your cup of coffee

00:30:32.620 --> 00:30:34.180
You're a disturbing sort of girl.

00:30:48.020 --> 00:30:48.760
It's getting late.

00:30:50.370 --> 00:30:50.990
Don't go yet.

00:30:51.810 --> 00:30:53.030
Oh, I wasn't going back tonight.

00:30:56.280 --> 00:30:57.640
If I won't be any bother to you.

00:30:58.100 --> 00:30:59.980
But remember, you got to go.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.020
You've got to treat me like a fella.

00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:43.320
Never knew bacon could taste so good.

00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:44.340
Funny, ain't it?

00:31:45.420 --> 00:31:46.980
Only yesterday there wasn't any used.

00:31:48.180 --> 00:31:49.560
We ain't said much to each other.

00:31:49.780 --> 00:31:50.880
Ain't said anything, really.

00:31:52.610 --> 00:31:56.300
Only, already yesterday seems way back there.

00:31:57.010 --> 00:31:58.390
Hey, let's get acquainted.

00:31:58.990 --> 00:31:59.390
All right.

00:32:01.690 --> 00:32:04.490
I'm Ellen Colby, and I hail from the mountains of Kentucky.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:07.200
Colby.

00:32:08.380 --> 00:32:11.010
What's the matter? Why do you look at me like that?

00:32:14.900 --> 00:32:17.930
I'm from the mountains of Kentucky. I'm Lynn Hayden.

00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:26.920
Ellen, listen, Ellen. It isn't our fight. We didn't start it.

00:32:27.370 --> 00:32:28.630
Why should we hate each other?

00:32:28.960 --> 00:32:29.980
My father went to jail.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:37.340
jail. Fifteen years he was there. Hayden sent him. Hayden went squealin' to the law.

00:32:38.330 --> 00:32:39.030
But I didn't then.

00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:46.130
Don't touch me! I don't wanna see you or any Hayden, except in a dead one.

00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:23.300
a farmer had two sons and these two sons were brothers

00:33:27.310 --> 00:33:29.410
gotta give me a kiss first

00:33:33.140 --> 00:33:35.560
I did have one for you, Ted, but it looks like it's cool.

00:33:35.840 --> 00:33:39.220
Oh, hunkus, boys, every day you'll see us.

00:33:39.220 --> 00:33:39.720
There you are.

00:33:40.240 --> 00:33:41.520
It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:33:41.640 --> 00:33:41.780
It's real, sir.

00:33:41.780 --> 00:33:43.920
Now these hunkus are dead and gone long way.

00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:49.080
They're actually a score hunkus of the paradise.

00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:51.380
You'll see the fire's way.

00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:53.380
I thought they were last year ago.

00:33:54.210 --> 00:33:55.330
Where did you find them, Lynn?

00:33:55.930 --> 00:33:57.970
Up in the attic after Granny Spelman died.

00:33:59.080 --> 00:33:59.980
I remember seeing your house.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:04.500
them when I was a kid. My father gave them to me when I left the old country and came

00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:27.870
to America. I was 15 years old then. And now I have grandchildren. Can she talk? She ain't old enough yet. Did he bring you a present too? Sure did. Look at this.

00:34:31.920 --> 00:34:32.540
Isn't that pretty?

00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:34.590
Is he your Uncle Lin, too?

00:34:34.970 --> 00:34:36.270
No, he's my brother.

00:34:36.770 --> 00:34:38.250
Just like Tanny there is your brother.

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:39.770
Uncle Phil!

00:34:46.120 --> 00:34:47.580
You kick me again and you'll get hurt.

00:34:47.960 --> 00:34:48.380
Uncle Lin!

00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:56.260
Hey Lin, you better take these boots away from your nephew before he gets hurt.

00:34:57.060 --> 00:34:57.520
Right there!

00:34:58.580 --> 00:34:59.980
Must have taken every dollar you...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.260
you have to buy all these present

00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:04.600
i figured i might land a job when i got here

00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:07.060
that won't be written for you a long time

00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:10.000
hope you're planning to settle down to it

00:35:10.350 --> 00:35:11.190
and get married

00:35:13.160 --> 00:35:15.120
finder raised on the ranches out here

00:35:15.120 --> 00:35:21.790
i think i've got one all picked out then

00:35:31.210 --> 00:35:32.630
What do you think of my big brother, Molly?

00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:36.420
This is very nice, Lynn, and I thank you.

00:35:36.660 --> 00:35:37.140
You're welcome.

00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:43.790
I'm glad you're back in the family, Lynn.

00:35:48.060 --> 00:35:49.880
Now, you leave things alone that don't belong to you.

00:35:56.580 --> 00:35:57.260
Never mind.

00:35:59.300 --> 00:35:59.700
And...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.380
How long have the Colby's been out here?

00:36:03.050 --> 00:36:04.030
Why, about a year.

00:36:04.590 --> 00:36:05.210
How'd you know?

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:08.840
I ran across Ellen Colby.

00:36:11.860 --> 00:36:12.700
She's white trash.

00:36:13.450 --> 00:36:14.990
Runs around with anyone that'll go with her.

00:36:15.050 --> 00:36:15.790
How do you know?

00:36:16.440 --> 00:36:17.420
She's some wild.

00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:20.160
She's young yet.

00:36:28.860 --> 00:36:29.800
Colby bothering Dad.

00:36:30.800 --> 00:36:32.040
Stealing cattle, that's all.

00:36:32.390 --> 00:36:33.170
Why, last year, Dad...

00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:33.270
No.

00:36:34.980 --> 00:36:36.480
Well, might as well know it sometime.

00:36:37.580 --> 00:36:38.840
Things are heading for a showdown.

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:41.310
Dad's still trying to sidestep a feud?

00:36:42.080 --> 00:36:43.020
Yes, if he can.

00:36:43.500 --> 00:36:45.080
But Neil and I don't feel that way about it.

00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:23.700
too far i can't reach him with this gun

00:37:24.140 --> 00:37:25.100
let's go after him

00:37:27.340 --> 00:37:29.440
that ought to stir him up enough to suit colby

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:31.820
Hayden will think I shot to kill that kid.

00:37:36.590 --> 00:37:38.490
Dad, you can't hold back on the Colby's this way.

00:37:38.960 --> 00:37:40.100
And you might as well know it now.

00:37:40.100 --> 00:37:41.720
The rest of the family can't understand it either.

00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:44.220
We are not going to feud to oblige Colby.

00:37:44.630 --> 00:37:46.550
They just shot at your own grandchild, didn't they?

00:37:46.770 --> 00:37:47.830
How are you going to answer that?

00:37:48.380 --> 00:37:51.300
When the time comes, I'll deal with Colby as a cattle thief.

00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:53.580
They didn't mean to hit Mary.

00:37:54.830 --> 00:37:57.590
Colby had that shot fired so we'd all fall into a trap.

00:37:58.150 --> 00:37:59.590
And he could wipe us out himself.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.970
defense. I've settled this my way.

00:38:03.170 --> 00:38:27.490
What do you think of them, Lynn? Great.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:30.260
Well?

00:38:31.380 --> 00:38:31.720
Well, what?

00:38:32.990 --> 00:38:33.590
Take your pick.

00:38:34.240 --> 00:38:35.220
That's what I brought him in for.

00:38:36.510 --> 00:38:38.450
You're not the only Santa Claus around this ranch.

00:38:39.810 --> 00:38:42.450
That white one over there.

00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:45.370
Just as I thought.

00:38:47.490 --> 00:38:47.990
White Cloud.

00:38:59.180 --> 00:38:59.900
What'd you call him?

00:39:00.160 --> 00:39:03.550
White Cloud. That's what he looks like, running against the side of a hill.

00:39:07.360 --> 00:39:09.290
I certainly appreciate him, Bill.

00:39:10.750 --> 00:39:14.270
You know, if it wasn't Sonya's suppertime, White Cloud and I would take a look at Dad's ranch.

00:39:15.240 --> 00:39:18.240
You'd better save that until morning, Lynn. It's an all-day ride.

00:39:43.020 --> 00:39:44.040
Where are you riding, Lynn?

00:39:44.680 --> 00:39:46.020
Oh, just looking around.

00:39:49.170 --> 00:39:50.630
You're going all day, won't you?

00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:53.890
Tell them Kobe's all right.

00:39:54.590 --> 00:39:56.670
It ain't her fault she's got a killing father.

00:39:57.370 --> 00:39:58.650
How'd you know I was going there?

00:39:59.030 --> 00:39:59.670
I saw yesterday.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.220
you were as lonely for her.

00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:02.680
I can't forget her, Molly.

00:40:02.880 --> 00:40:03.970
You shouldn't.

00:40:04.720 --> 00:40:05.780
It's more important

00:40:05.780 --> 00:40:06.340
than anything

00:40:06.340 --> 00:40:07.080
the Haydens

00:40:07.080 --> 00:40:07.840
or the Colbys

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:08.820
could be fighting about.

00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:11.850
You won't be telling

00:40:11.850 --> 00:40:12.350
on me, will you?

00:40:13.310 --> 00:40:13.710
No.

00:40:13.850 --> 00:40:14.950
The last time

00:40:14.950 --> 00:40:14.970
I saw you,

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:19.960
I saw of you, you was riding out that one.

00:43:21.810 --> 00:43:26.120
It struck me funny, Mark Hayden chasing you out of Grass Valley.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.960
see you laughing last night when they chased

00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:34.000
you off his ranch. We're going back

00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:34.360
tonight.

00:43:35.148 --> 00:43:35.488
Hmm.

00:43:36.524 --> 00:43:38.064
I figured something like that.

00:43:41.196 --> 00:43:42.256
I'll handle it myself.

00:43:42.860 --> 00:43:43.420
This time.

00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:38.510
Just before daybreak, they stole all your horses, Bill, and took all the cattle out of the south pasture.

00:44:40.880 --> 00:44:41.700
Get him up to the house.

00:45:01.020 --> 00:45:01.540
Colby's?

00:45:02.720 --> 00:45:03.120
Yeah.

00:45:05.040 --> 00:45:05.900
Don't say anything to Dad.

00:45:06.540 --> 00:45:08.920
I'm going up in the Colby's neighborhood and try to locate that stock.

00:45:09.570 --> 00:45:11.610
You have every hand on the ranch ready when I come back.

00:45:11.910 --> 00:45:13.290
No matter what anybody says.

00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:15.430
We're all going after what belongs to us.

00:46:09.150 --> 00:46:12.390
You needn't say anything to Colby about us planting gunpowder up here.

00:46:14.100 --> 00:46:16.420
He doesn't want to handle the Haydens my way, huh?

00:46:18.140 --> 00:46:19.960
We'll drive out the rest of their stock tonight.

00:46:20.400 --> 00:46:23.100
That'll get every man of them coming after us up through this canyon.

00:46:25.420 --> 00:46:26.300
One little match.

00:46:28.590 --> 00:46:29.030
Wham!

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:35.620
I hope Colby ain't in the canyon at the same time.

00:46:40.180 --> 00:46:41.780
Hey, do you want to see something interesting?

00:46:42.880 --> 00:46:43.260
Come here.

00:47:02.840 --> 00:47:03.920
Take care of a white cloud.

00:48:27.930 --> 00:48:28.770
I'm in Haydn, I'm afraid.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.940
And then he give you and you the beating of your lives.

00:48:33.676 --> 00:48:35.116
But I'm not allowing you to say,

00:48:35.564 --> 00:48:37.144
That Ellen's been making up to him.

00:48:53.004 --> 00:48:54.004
You get her this?

00:49:00.956 --> 00:49:02.956
Is that your handwriting?

00:49:08.316 --> 00:49:10.376
Have every man settle up and meet me at the corrals.

00:49:11.804 --> 00:49:12.564
Well, get going.

00:49:35.244 --> 00:49:37.784
Have you been accepting favors from Lynn Hayden?

00:49:39.116 --> 00:49:40.356
I'm going to marry Lynn Hayden.

00:49:41.100 --> 00:49:42.020
In that dress.

00:50:08.988 --> 00:50:09.488
Yeah!

00:50:09.980 --> 00:50:10.480
Yeah!

00:50:11.388 --> 00:50:14.148
If you want fried chicken for supper, you better get your hatchet.

00:50:36.748 --> 00:50:37.248
Woo!

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.000
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:52:01.690 --> 00:52:02.770
I don't know.

00:53:30.990 --> 00:53:31.170
Thank you.

00:54:47.310 --> 00:54:52.880
Bill's outside, and his horse dead.

00:54:58.540 --> 00:54:59.840
Well, you want me to bring him in?

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:05.290
you run and tell the sheriff because it wouldn't be fair to accuse a Colby

00:55:05.290 --> 00:55:16.320
that's when you knew for certain maybe you want to look make sure all right ahead

00:55:21.780 --> 00:55:29.960
that's Bill same face the same hand the same eyes that have been look

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:37.060
looking at you ever since they first opened, only they're closed now, and they're never

00:55:37.060 --> 00:55:48.130
going to open anymore. Never! Molly, stop it. Calm yourself. Oh, I'm calm. I'm just telling

00:55:48.130 --> 00:55:55.320
you to do your duty. It's your move, ain't it? The Colbys killed the Haydens, and the

00:55:55.320 --> 00:55:59.960
Haydens tell the law. Ain't that the game? Ain't that the rules?

00:56:00.760 --> 00:56:04.960
Only you better hurry. Better send quick for help.

00:56:05.520 --> 00:56:07.180
Because maybe they'll start shooting their children.

00:56:07.360 --> 00:56:10.040
And the children ain't old enough. They wouldn't know enough to run.

00:56:13.560 --> 00:56:14.240
Still gonna...

00:56:16.190 --> 00:56:19.150
Ben go to the law like you did when he killed old man Spellman.

00:57:13.500 --> 00:57:29.970
Hey, I guess plug Mark Hayden. I'm figuring the rest of his outfit will be longer any minute. We'd better be moving. Yeah, we wait for him at the end of the road

00:57:30.640 --> 00:57:34.870
They'll follow us. Come on, fellas, let's go.

01:02:06.780 --> 01:02:07.520
Lynn, you've got to get up.

01:02:07.932 --> 01:02:09.532
Hurry! Lynn, you've got to get out of here.

01:02:09.732 --> 01:02:10.532
Lynn, come on.

01:02:57.964 --> 01:02:58.804
Stay with you.

01:03:08.988 --> 01:03:10.868
You'll have to depend on me from now on, Ellen.

01:03:11.484 --> 01:03:15.104
Your father and the rest of them got caught in a landslide up in the canyon.

01:03:17.788 --> 01:03:19.088
Lenheden, too.

01:03:21.212 --> 01:03:22.592
You sure Lynn Hayden was killed?

01:03:24.156 --> 01:03:25.156
Yes.

01:03:28.412 --> 01:03:29.132
I don't believe you.

01:03:32.172 --> 01:03:33.212
It's just you and needless.

01:03:34.604 --> 01:03:35.444
We're getting married.

01:03:42.316 --> 01:03:43.896
You ain't serious about that.

01:03:44.332 --> 01:03:46.192
Sure, sure. What'd you think?

01:03:49.996 --> 01:03:51.996
I didn't know you thought of me that way.

01:03:54.124 --> 01:03:55.124
changed some lately.

01:04:01.530 --> 01:04:07.480
Well, if you're proposing, do I have to give my answer right away?

01:04:08.510 --> 01:04:10.740
Why not? We'll get along.

01:04:11.560 --> 01:04:14.710
We'll be the biggest ranchers in this state, will you say?

01:04:30.350 --> 01:04:30.550
Thank you.
